  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "The Hub – a wall pass via the centre line and a finish off the corner pass",
  "description": "Half court, one goal with a goalkeeper. The line stands in the left corner, B with the balls in the right corner and D at the centre line by the right boards. A, first in line, moves out towards the middle of the zone and gets a pass from B. A plays it out diagonally to D, who returns it first time. A then passes back to B in the corner and gets in front of goal, where B lays it on and A shoots first time.\n\nRotation: the shooter stays on as the new passer in the right corner, and B goes round behind the goal to the line in the left corner. Change the player at the centre line every few minutes, and run it mirrored too.\n\nVariant: every pass is one touch. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Receive the ball on the move – don't stop in the middle."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Open your body to the next pass before the ball arrives."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "A: drift away first before coming in front of goal, to open up free space."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Shoot first time off the pass from the corner."
    }
  ],
